---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ObfuscatedEmail from '../../components/ObfuscatedEmail.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Transportation Committee" description="BWNA's Transportation Committee identifies and advocates for Beaumont-Wilshire's transportation concerns, with pedestrian, cyclist, and driver safety as its priority.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Transportation Committee</h1>
      <p>Safer streets for walking, biking, and driving in Beaumont-Wilshire</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container content-width">
      <p>
        This committee works to identify and advocate for the transportation-related concerns of
        our neighborhood. Pedestrian, cyclist, and driver safety are their priority. The
        committee brings its concerns to the attention of the Portland Bureau of Transportation
        to seek solutions.
      </p>

      <div class="map-callout">
        <h2>Neighborhood Transportation Map</h2>
        <p>
          Explore greenways, Safe Routes to School, High Crash Network streets, and crash records
          across Beaumont-Wilshire on the committee's interactive map.
        </p>
        <a href={`${base}transportation-map`} class="btn btn-secondary">View the map</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container content-width">
      <h2>Getting to Know Your BWNA Transportation Volunteer</h2>
      <p>
        Hi neighbors, my name is Graeme Rudd. I recently volunteered to support the BWNA in a
        transportation role, and I wanted to introduce myself and share a bit about what I've
        been working on.
      </p>

      <h3>A little about me</h3>
      <p>
        I spent about 14 years working for the federal government in a variety of roles, mostly
        in the military. I served as a Green Beret, and part of that work included time with a
        technology lab and as an intelligence analyst, where I spent a lot of time working with
        geographic information systems (GIS). That background shapes how I'm approaching this
        role: I like to start by getting a clear picture of what's actually happening on the
        ground.
      </p>

      <h3>Why I'm doing this</h3>
      <p>
        We often hear that there's no money right now for many of the transportation
        improvements our neighborhood needs. At the same time, I've become aware that there may
        be funding allocations or programs out there. So my first goal has been simple: get a
        better understanding of our neighborhood's transportation picture, and find out what
        resources might be available.
      </p>

      <h3>What I've been working on</h3>
      <p>
        So far I've had two helpful conversations with PBOT (the Portland Bureau of
        Transportation). I learned a lot, and they pointed me to data that has helped me
        understand what's going on in our area and where I need to dig deeper.
      </p>
      <p>I've also started putting that data onto an interactive map. It shows things like:</p>
      <ul class="spaced-list">
        <li>Where our greenways are</li>
        <li>Roads on the High Crash Network (Fremont, for example, is one)</li>
        <li>Safe Routes to School</li>
        <li>The intersections that crash data shows are most dangerous</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        My hope is to build this out into something neighbors can explore, so we all have a
        shared understanding of what we're looking at.
      </p>

      <h3>Where this could lead</h3>
      <p>
        Once we have a clearer picture, I'd like to see whether any of our needs line up with
        existing programs that could help fund improvements, such as Safe Routes to School. At
        the very least, this work should help us show PBOT and our elected representatives where
        our neighborhood needs the most help.
      </p>

      <h3>How you can be part of it</h3>
      <p>
        Data only tells part of the story. I'm also working with other members of the committee
        on ways to gather community input and feedback, so we can present a more complete
        picture of our neighborhood. The goal is for us to advocate for what the community needs
        most with data and insights to support our communications.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'll share more as the map comes together. In the meantime, if you have thoughts about
        transportation in the neighborhood, I'd love to hear them.
      </p>
      <p>Best,<br />Graeme</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container content-width">
      <h2>Get involved</h2>
      <p>
        If you're interested in assisting with the important work of this committee,
        <ObfuscatedEmail email="pdx.stmptwn@gmail.com" label="contact the Transportation Committee Chair" />.
      </p>
      <p><a href={`${base}committees`}>&larr; All committees</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .content-width > h2:not(:first-child) {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }

  .content-width > h3:not(:first-child) {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .map-callout {
    background: var(--color-primary-light);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin: var(--spacing-xl) 0;
  }

  .map-callout h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
